Spec: SystemInstance

Purpose:
  Carry the full cluster-side contract of one system-package installation: declare the install
    coordinate (`jukebox`, `category`, `package`, opaque `options`), track per-stage install
    progress and child inventory in @SystemInstanceStatus through @ApplicationCondition records,
    provide the status mutators awaited by the install flow and its Rhai scripts, and register
    @SystemInstance with its full accessor and mutator bridge onto package @rhai::Engine
    instances.

Owns:
  ./instancesystem.rs

Must:
  The @kube::CustomResource derive over @SystemInstanceSpec generates the @SystemInstance
    resource kind `SystemInstance` in group `vynil.solidite.fr`, version `v1`, namespaced
    scope, shortname `vsi`, plural `systeminstances`, with status type @SystemInstanceStatus and
    CRD doc `Custom resource representing an Vynil cluster package installation`.
  The CRD printer columns are, in order and by `jsonPath`: `Juke` -> `.spec.jukebox`,
    `cat` -> `.spec.category`, `pkg` -> `.spec.package`, `tag` -> `.status.tag`,
    `last_updated` -> `.status.conditions[?(@.type == 'Ready')].lastTransitionTime`
    (column type `date`, format `date-time`; the other six columns are type `string`),
    `stage` -> `.status.conditions[-1:].type`,
    `errors` -> `.status.conditions[?(@.status == 'False')].message`.
  Wire keys are fixed: the spec keys are `jukebox`, `category`, `package`, `options`; the
    status keys are `conditions`, `tag`, `digest`, `tfstate`, `rhaistate`, `systems`, `crds`;
    @ApplicationCondition serializes camelCase keys `lastTransitionTime`, `message`, `type`
    (fixed by the @serde rename on @ApplicationCondition::condition_type), `status`,
    `generation`; @ConditionsType and @ConditionsStatus serialize as bare variant strings.
  Every @ApplicationCondition stamps @chrono::Utc::now() into `lastTransitionTime` and the
    caller-supplied generation at construction; a condition carried across a later patch keeps
    its original timestamp.
  Each status mutator reads `metadata.generation` and uses `1` when absent, rebuilds
    `status.conditions` from the existing conditions minus the types it excludes, then appends
    its fresh conditions (@SystemInstance::get_conditions_excluding), and finally patches the
    `status` subresource as a @kube::api::Patch::Merge carrying `apiVersion`
    `vynil.solidite.fr/v1` and the kind string `SystemInstance` — the @impl_instance_common!
    call-site literal — so the server replaces only the keys present in the patch, omitted
    keys keep their stored values, and an included `conditions` array is replaced wholesale.
  Each mutator returns the `@Ok` value of its status patch, not the locally mutated value:
    a successful patch publishes its event, a failed patch or an unsuppressed event-publish
    error returns `Err` and publishes nothing.
  @SystemInstance::set_status_ready removes every `AgentStarted`, `Ready` and `Installed`
    condition, appends @ApplicationCondition::ready_ok and @ApplicationCondition::installed_ok
    (message `Installed succesfully` for both), and patches `conditions`, `tag`, and `digest`
    — the digest is @sha256::digest of the @serde_json serialization of
    @SystemInstanceSpec::options, or @sha256::digest of `""` when options are absent — then
    publishes a `Normal` event with reason `InstallSucceed` and action `Install`.
  @SystemInstance::set_status_systems replaces only the `SystemApplied` condition with
    @ApplicationCondition::system_ok (message `Templates applied succesfully`, always this fixed
    text, never the children), patches `conditions` and `systems`, and publishes a `Normal`
    event with reason `SystemApplySucceed`, action `SystemApply`, note
    `Applied {count} Objects` where `count` is the length of the input list.
  @SystemInstance::set_status_system_failed removes `AgentStarted`, `SystemApplied` and
    `Installed`, appends @ApplicationCondition::system_ko and @ApplicationCondition::installed_ko
    both carrying the full reason, and appends @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko only when no
    `Ready`-type condition survives the rebuild — presence is matched by type alone, ignoring
    generation and current status — then patches `conditions` only and publishes a `Warning`
    event with reason `SystemApplyFailed` and action `SystemApply` whose note is the reason
    truncated to 1023 bytes.
  @SystemInstance::have_child answers `true` exactly when a status is present and at least one
    probe succeeds: `rhaistate` is `@Some` or `tfstate` is `@Some` regardless of content, or
    `systems` or `crds` is `@Some` and non-empty; probes are evaluated in that order and short
    circuit.
  Every Rhai-facing synchronous bridge — @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_systems,
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_system_failed, and the wrappers the instance macros attach —
    drives its async operation through @tokio::task::block_in_place combined with
    @tokio::runtime::Handle::block_on, so it must run on a multi-thread runtime
    (@tokio::task::block_in_place panics on a current-thread runtime) and converts any failure
    through @crate::rhai_err into a string-carrying @rhai error, losing the @crate::Error
    variant.
  @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_systems converts its @rhai::Dynamic argument by a
    @serde_json string round-trip into `Vec<@crate::Children>` before delegating; an argument
    that does not deserialize to that shape fails without touching the cluster.

Depends on:
  @impl_condition_common! and @impl_condition_crds! in ./instance_macros.rs — stamp
    @ApplicationCondition::new with @chrono::Utc::now and supply the generation-carrying
    constructors the in-file setters compose, including @ApplicationCondition::ready_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko, @ApplicationCondition::installed_ok and
    @ApplicationCondition::installed_ko.
  @impl_instance_common!(SystemInstance, "SystemInstance") in ./instance_macros.rs — attach the
    status merge-patch (@SystemInstance::patch_status, embedding the call-site kind literal),
    the event recorder (@SystemInstance::send_event, which reports `kube::Error::Api` publish
    failures as warnings and returns `@Ok`), the private
    @SystemInstance::get_conditions_excluding rebuild helper this file's setters call, and the
    shared lookup, options-digest, tfstate/rhaistate, agent/missing, and CRD-agnostic Rhai
    surface that @system_rhai_register republishes.
  @impl_instance_crds!(SystemInstance) in ./instance_macros.rs — attach the CRD-stage setters
    @SystemInstance::set_status_crds and @SystemInstance::set_status_crd_failed with their Rhai
    wrappers, completing the condition stages @ConditionsType::CrdApplied names.
  @crate::context::get_client_async in ./context.rs — every mutating call fetches the shared
    @kube::Client from context at call time; nothing stores a client in the resource.
  @crate::Children in ./lib.rs — the child object records stored in `status.systems` and
    deserialized out of the @rhai::Dynamic argument.
  @crate::Error, @crate::Result, @crate::RhaiRes and @crate::rhai_err in ./lib.rs — the error
    contract propagated by the async setters and flattened to strings at the Rhai bridges.
  @kube::CustomResource, @kube::Resource, @kube::ResourceExt — the derive that generates
    @SystemInstance and the metadata/object-ref plumbing behind the macro-owned patching and
    event recording.
  @rhai::Engine and @rhai::Dynamic — the engine this file registers the bridge onto and the
    argument type accepted from package scripts.

Exposes:
  @SystemInstanceSpec — CRD spec struct with public fields @SystemInstanceSpec::jukebox,
    @SystemInstanceSpec::category, @SystemInstanceSpec::package and
    @SystemInstanceSpec::options (`@Option<@serde_json::Map<@String, @serde_json::Value>>`);
    derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema.
  @SystemInstance — resource root generated by the @kube::CustomResource derive over
    @SystemInstanceSpec, with fields `spec` (@SystemInstanceSpec) and `status`
    (`@Option<@SystemInstanceStatus>`); derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Clone, @Debug and
    @JsonSchema via the derive.
  @ConditionsType — install-stage enum, exactly one variant per recorded stage: `Ready`,
    `Installed`, `AgentStarted`, `CrdApplied`, `TofuInstalled`, `SystemApplied`, `RhaiApplied`;
    derives @Serialize and @Deserialize as unit strings, @Eq and @PartialEq, @Clone, @Debug,
    @JsonSchema, and @Default selecting `Ready`.
  @ConditionsStatus — enum `True` or `False`, serialized as those strings, with @Default
    selecting `True`; derives @Eq and @PartialEq, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema.
  @ApplicationCondition — one recorded condition with public fields
    @ApplicationCondition::last_transition_time (`@Option<@chrono::DateTime<@chrono::Utc>>`),
    @ApplicationCondition::message, @ApplicationCondition::condition_type,
    @ApplicationCondition::status and @ApplicationCondition::generation (`@i64`); derives
    @Eq and @PartialEq, compared field-by-field by the macro-owned dedup gate.
  @ApplicationCondition::system_ko and @ApplicationCondition::system_ok — this module's
    SystemApplied-stage constructors.
  Constructors attached by @impl_condition_common!: @ApplicationCondition::new,
    @ApplicationCondition::ready_ok, @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::installed_ok, @ApplicationCondition::installed_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::agent_started, @ApplicationCondition::missing_package,
    @ApplicationCondition::missing_box, @ApplicationCondition::missing_requirement,
    @ApplicationCondition::tofu_ok, @ApplicationCondition::tofu_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::rhai_ok, @ApplicationCondition::rhai_ko.
  Constructors attached by @impl_condition_crds!: @ApplicationCondition::crd_ok and
    @ApplicationCondition::crd_ko for @ConditionsType::CrdApplied.
  @SystemInstanceStatus — status struct with public fields @SystemInstanceStatus::conditions,
    @SystemInstanceStatus::tag, @SystemInstanceStatus::digest, @SystemInstanceStatus::tfstate,
    @SystemInstanceStatus::rhaistate, @SystemInstanceStatus::systems
    (`@Option<@Vec<@crate::Children>>`) and @SystemInstanceStatus::crds
    (`@Option<@Vec<@String>>`); derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema.
  @SystemInstance::have_child — child-state probe.
  @SystemInstance::set_status_ready, @SystemInstance::set_status_systems and
    @SystemInstance::set_status_system_failed — the async system-stage status mutators.
  @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_systems and @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_system_failed —
    the synchronous Rhai bridges over those two mutators.
  Methods attached by @impl_instance_common!: async @SystemInstance::get, @SystemInstance::list,
    @SystemInstance::get_options_digest, @SystemInstance::get_tfstate,
    @SystemInstance::get_rhaistate, @SystemInstance::set_tfstate,
    @SystemInstance::set_status_tofu_failed, @SystemInstance::set_rhaistate,
    @SystemInstance::set_status_rhai_failed, @SystemInstance::set_agent_started,
    @SystemInstance::set_missing_box, @SystemInstance::set_missing_package and
    @SystemInstance::set_missing_requirement; Rhai bridges @SystemInstance::rhai_get,
    @SystemInstance::rhai_list, @SystemInstance::get_metadata, @SystemInstance::get_spec,
    @SystemInstance::get_status, @SystemInstance::rhai_get_tfstate,
    @SystemInstance::rhai_get_rhaistate, @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_ready,
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_tfstate, @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_tofu_failed,
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_rhaistate, @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_rhai_failed,
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_agent_started, @SystemInstance::rhai_set_missing_box,
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_missing_package and @SystemInstance::rhai_set_missing_requirement.
  Methods attached by @impl_instance_crds!: @SystemInstance::set_status_crds,
    @SystemInstance::set_status_crd_failed, @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_crds and
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_crd_failed.
  @system_rhai_register — installs the script-visible surface on a caller @rhai::Engine under
    the registered type name `SystemInstance`: free functions `get_system_instance` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_get, `list_system_instance` -> @SystemInstance::rhai_list,
    `options_digest` -> @SystemInstance::get_options_digest, `get_tfstate` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_get_tfstate, `get_rhaistate` -> @SystemInstance::rhai_get_rhaistate,
    `set_agent_started` -> @SystemInstance::rhai_set_agent_started, `set_missing_box` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_missing_box, `set_missing_package` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_missing_package, `set_missing_requirement` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_missing_requirement, `set_status_ready` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_ready, `set_status_crds` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_crds, `set_status_crd_failed` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_crd_failed, `set_status_systems` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_systems, `set_status_system_failed` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_system_failed, `set_tfstate` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_tfstate, `set_status_tofu_failed` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_tofu_failed, `set_rhaistate` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_rhaistate, `set_status_rhai_failed` ->
    @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_rhai_failed; property getters `metadata` ->
    @SystemInstance::get_metadata, `spec` -> @SystemInstance::get_spec, `status` ->
    @SystemInstance::get_status.

Accepts:
  Install coordinates as free-form strings in @SystemInstanceSpec::jukebox,
    @SystemInstanceSpec::category and @SystemInstanceSpec::package, plus
    @SystemInstanceSpec::options as any JSON object map or @None — this file only digests
    `options`, it never interprets its contents.
  @SystemInstance::set_status_ready takes the installed `tag`: @String.
  @SystemInstance::set_status_systems takes the applied `systems`: `@Vec<@crate::Children>`.
  @SystemInstance::set_status_system_failed takes a human-readable `reason`: @String, with no
    length or charset validation.
  @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_systems takes any @rhai::Dynamic that must JSON-round-trip
    into `Vec<@crate::Children>` (camelCase keys `apiVersion`, `kind`, `name`, `namespace`).
  @system_rhai_register takes a borrowed @rhai::Engine to decorate.

Returns:
  Each async setter returns @crate::Result<@SystemInstance> whose `@Ok` carries the
    server-merged @SystemInstance read back from @SystemInstance::patch_status.
  The two in-file Rhai bridges return @crate::RhaiRes<@SystemInstance> wrapping the same object.
  @SystemInstance::have_child returns a `@bool` per the probe rules above.
  The registered `get_tfstate`/`get_rhaistate` return the decoded state string, or `""` when
    no state is stored (@SystemInstance::rhai_get_tfstate and
    @SystemInstance::rhai_get_rhaistate default the `@None`).
  The registered `options_digest` returns the hex digest string directly, not a `@Result`.
  The registered property getters return @rhai::Dynamic, and `status` is Rhai null when
    @SystemInstanceStatus is `@None`.

Raises:
  @crate::Error::KubeError from @SystemInstance::patch_status when the status subresource call
    fails — every async setter propagates it through `?`.
  @crate::Error::KubeError from event publishing when @SystemInstance::send_event fails with a
    @kube::Error variant other than `Api`.
  @crate::Error::SerializationError when @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_systems cannot convert
    its @rhai::Dynamic argument.
  Every Rhai bridge instead returns a @rhai::EvalAltResult produced by @crate::rhai_err — the
    typed @crate::Error is flattened into its message string.

Handles:
  Missing `metadata.generation` — recorded and defaulted to `1` by every setter and
    constructor.
  @SystemInstanceStatus absent, or `conditions` empty — the condition rebuild starts from an
    empty set instead of failing.
  A `Ready` condition already present when @SystemInstance::set_status_system_failed runs — it
    is carried through and no @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko is appended.
  @SystemInstanceSpec::options absent — @SystemInstance::set_status_ready still writes a
    `digest` (of the empty string).
  Failure reason longer than 1023 bytes — the event note is truncated while the stored condition
    `message` keeps the full reason.
  Event publishing answering a `kube::Error::Api` (for example on a terminating namespace) —
    @SystemInstance::send_event logs it as a warning and the setter still completes `@Ok`.

Tasks:
  [ ] No in-file @tests module exists, so none of the Scenarios below has a mapping test yet;
      cover them from these Scenario blocks under the project TTD rule when test work starts.
  [?] @SystemInstance::set_status_system_failed selects the @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko
      append by matching surviving conditions on type @ConditionsType::Ready only, ignoring
      generation and @ConditionsStatus — a `Ready`/`True` from an older generation survives a
      later failure, keeping the printed Ready column green while `Installed` turns `False`.
      Decide later whether the match must also consider generation or status. The same pattern
      exists in the macro-owned failure setters.
  [?] @SystemInstance::set_status_system_failed truncates the event note by byte index with
      @str::truncate(`1023`), which panics when the byte falls inside a multi-byte character of
      a non-ASCII reason. Decide later whether truncation must be char-safe. The same pattern
      exists in the macro-owned setters.
  [?] @SystemInstance::set_status_ready and @SystemInstance::set_status_system_failed remove
      every @ConditionsType::AgentStarted condition on each patch, so the agent-start trace
      never survives a later stage. Confirm this eviction is intended.
  [?] Wire-visible messages @ApplicationCondition::ready_ok and @ApplicationCondition::installed_ok
      both carry `Installed succesfully` and @ApplicationCondition::system_ok carries
      `Templates applied succesfully` (misspellings, duplicated text). They are recorded as-is;
      decide later whether corrected strings are an acceptable CRD-visible change.
  [?] @SystemInstance::have_child is asymmetric: `tfstate`/`rhaistate` as @Some of the empty
      string count as a child, while @Some of an empty list in `systems`/`crds` does not.
      Confirm the asymmetry is intended.
  [?] @SystemInstance::set_status_ready has no idempotence gate (unlike the have_condition gate
      in @SystemInstance::set_agent_started): a no-change re-run rewrites tag, digest, and
      conditions. Decide later whether an equality gate is wanted.
  [?] All Rhai bridges run async work through @tokio::task::block_in_place and
      @tokio::runtime::Handle::block_on and therefore panic on a current-thread runtime; typed
      @crate::Error is also flattened to a string at the bridge. Documented as behavior; decide
      later whether the runtime requirement must be enforced or the bridges redesigned.
  [?] Dérives @std::default::Default on @ConditionsType and @ConditionsStatus have no detectable
      use repo-wide. Decide later whether they stay.
  [?] The @SystemInstanceSpec struct doc `Describe a source of vynil packages jukebox` is
      inherited from the `JukeBox` model and does not describe this CRD (the CRD doc string
      itself is correct) — confirm the intended wording.

Done when:
  Every Scenario above has a passing in-file test and `cargo test -p common` is green.

Scenario: Ready install closes with tag and digest
  Given a @SystemInstance whose spec carries an options map, whose `metadata.generation` is
    absent, and whose status holds one `CrdApplied`/`True` condition recorded at generation `3`
  When @SystemInstance::set_status_ready is awaited with tag `1.2.3`
  Then the merged status carries `tag` `1.2.3` and a `digest` equal to the value
    @SystemInstance::get_options_digest returns for the same spec
  And the patched `conditions` are exactly the carried-over `CrdApplied` record plus fresh
    `Ready` and `Installed` conditions, both `True` at generation `1` with message
    `Installed succesfully`
  And a `Normal` event with reason `InstallSucceed` and action `Install` is published
  None of these Scenarios has an in-file test yet; see the open task above.

Scenario: Missing options still produces a digest
  Given a @SystemInstance with @SystemInstanceSpec::options set to @None
  When @SystemInstance::set_status_ready is awaited
  Then the patched `digest` is @sha256::digest of the empty string

Scenario: System apply records children, other stages untouched
  Given a @SystemInstance whose status holds `TofuInstalled`/`True`, `RhaiApplied`/`False` and a
    stale `SystemApplied` condition
  When @SystemInstance::set_status_systems is awaited with two @crate::Children entries
  Then the stale `SystemApplied` condition is replaced by one `True` condition of type
    `SystemApplied` with message `Templates applied succesfully`
  And the `TofuInstalled` and `RhaiApplied` records are carried over unchanged, timestamps
    included
  And `status.systems` holds exactly the two children and a `Normal` event is published with
    note `Applied 2 Objects`, reason `SystemApplySucceed`, action `SystemApply`

Scenario: System failure without a Ready condition marks all three
  Given a @SystemInstance whose status holds no `Ready`-type condition at any generation
  When @SystemInstance::set_status_system_failed is awaited with reason `boom`
  Then the patched `conditions` carry `SystemApplied`/`False` and `Installed`/`False` records
    with message `boom`, plus an appended `Ready`/`False` record with message
    `No successful install`
  And a `Warning` event is published with reason `SystemApplyFailed`, action `SystemApply` and
    note `boom`
  And the patched list drops every `AgentStarted` record, success or failure, along with any
    stale `SystemApplied` record

Scenario: System failure keeps a surviving Ready condition
  Given a @SystemInstance whose status holds a `Ready`/`True` condition recorded at generation
    `3` while `metadata.generation` now reads `4`
  When @SystemInstance::set_status_system_failed is awaited with reason `boom`
  Then no @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko is appended and the old `Ready`/`True` record at
    generation `3` is carried through, so the printed Ready column keeps reporting the stale
    success while `Installed` flips to `False`

Scenario: Mis-shaped Rhai children list is rejected before any patch
  Given a @rhai script calling the registered `set_status_systems` with a @rhai::Dynamic whose
    entries lack the `kind` and `name` fields of @crate::Children
  When @SystemInstance::rhai_set_status_systems runs
  Then the call returns a @rhai::EvalAltResult carrying the serialized
    @crate::Error::SerializationError message
  And no status patch or event is attempted

Scenario: Child-state probe
  Given a @SystemInstance with no status at all, @SystemInstance::have_child answers `false`
  But when only `rhaistate` or only `tfstate` is `@Some`, even the empty string, it answers
    `true`
  And when `systems` and `crds` are both `@Some` of empty lists and no state is stored, it
    answers `false`
  And when `crds` is `@Some` of one entry, it answers `true`
